Subject: [PATCH] clk: ingenic: t31: fix the MSC0/MSC1 divider

The T31 MSCxCDR divider is (CDR + 1) * 2, as on X1000/JZ4780
(x1000-cgu.c, jz4780-cgu.c) and as the Ingenic programming manual
states ("division ratio = (MSC0CDR + 1)*2"); the vendor 3.10 CGU uses
coe = 2 as well. The table used * 4, so the clock framework believes
the MSC runs at half its real rate: a 24 MHz request yields ~48 MHz on
the bus. Commands and short responses survive, but 512-byte data
blocks fail: an SD card enumerates without its partitions and an SDIO
WiFi function binds without bringing up its interface.

Seen on a Wuuk Y0510 (T31X, SD on MSC0, SSV6158 on MSC1); QEMU does
not model the divider and hides it.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/ingenic/t31-cgu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/ingenic/t31-cgu.c
@@ -273,14 +273,14 @@
 	[T31_CLK_MSC0] = {
 		"msc0", CGU_CLK_DIV | CGU_CLK_GATE,
 		.parents = { T31_CLK_MSCMUX, -1, -1, -1 },
-		.div = { CGU_REG_MSC0CDR, 0, 4, 8, 29, 28, 27 },
+		.div = { CGU_REG_MSC0CDR, 0, 2, 8, 29, 28, 27 },
 		.gate = { CGU_REG_CLKGR0, 4 },
 	},
 
 	[T31_CLK_MSC1] = {
 		"msc1", CGU_CLK_DIV | CGU_CLK_GATE,
 		.parents = { T31_CLK_MSCMUX, -1, -1, -1 },
-		.div = { CGU_REG_MSC1CDR, 0, 4, 8, 29, 28, 27 },
+		.div = { CGU_REG_MSC1CDR, 0, 2, 8, 29, 28, 27 },
 		.gate = { CGU_REG_CLKGR0, 5 },
 	},
 
